WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:11.560
Modern software depends on third-party libraries, open-source components, package managers, transitive dependencies, container images, build tools, source repositories, and CI/CD services.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:17.060
These components save time and improve capability, but they also become part of the product risk.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:25.120
A vulnerability, license issue, abandoned package, or unexpected behavior in a component the team did not write can still affect customers.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.740
Dependency freshness and ownership matter.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:37.480
Teams should know which components are used, who owns upgrades, how vulnerability alerts are triaged, and what happens when a dependency is no longer maintained.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:41.940
Transitive dependencies deserve attention because they may enter the product indirectly.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:47.920
If nobody is responsible for reviewing or updating them, supply chain risk accumulates quietly.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:55.020
Vulnerability scanning, license review, provenance concepts, and software bills of materials all support supply chain hygiene.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:00.280
Scanning can identify known issues, but findings need triage and remediation.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:04.900
Provenance helps teams understand where software came from and whether it should be trusted.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:12.800
An SBOM, at a high level, provides visibility into the components included in a product or system so response is based on inventory.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:18.460
Supply chain security is part of the secure SDLC because it starts before release and continues after deployment.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:29.640
Teams should avoid unnecessary components, use trusted sources, control registry and repository access, protect build systems, review container images, and document exceptions.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:32.500
The goal is not to ban third-party software.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.560
The goal is to use it deliberately, with evidence and ownership.
